course: dictionary
lesson: 2765
title: Formal words for stop
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Discontinue means to stop doing, making or providing something. «The shop has discontinued that toy.» The toy is no longer on sale, so the shop has stopped selling it. You can check this with the clues: a shop that has stopped selling a toy is not going to keep making it.
explain: Discontinue is a formal word. You will often see it in notices, letters and exam questions, where it is a stiffer way of saying stop. «The service will be discontinued.» This means the service is going to come to an end. Stop and discontinue mean nearly the same, but discontinue sounds more official.
explain: Look for the word patterns that go with it. You can discontinue a service, or discontinue the use of something, such as an old app or a machine. In each case, someone has decided to end it. When you meet the word in a notice, ask yourself: what has stopped, and who has decided it?
fact: Discontinue means to stop doing, making or providing something.
fact: «Discontinued» means no longer made or offered.
fact: A «discontinued line» is a product that a company has stopped making.
fact: You can discontinue a service, or discontinue the use of something, such as a product or an app.
fact: Discontinue is a formal word for stop, so you will often see it in notices and letters.
exercise: «The shop has discontinued that toy.» What does discontinued mean here? | Wrapped up as a present | Made bigger and better | Sold at half price | *Stopped making or selling
exercise: In a formal notice, which word means the same as discontinue? | Repeat | Begin | *Stop | Continue
exercise: «The service will be discontinued.» What will happen to the service? | *It will come to an end | It will be shared with the school | It will be given to a new company | It will be made faster
test: Which phrase means that a company has stopped making a product? | Free sample | A brand-new wrapper | *A discontinued line | Just launched
test: A notice says, «Please discontinue the use of this app.» What should you do? | *Stop using the app | Download it again | Tell your friends to use it | Update it every day
exam: «The firm will discontinue the old phone.» Which word could replace discontinue without changing the meaning? | Polish | Repair | Advertise | *Stop making
